 ## 3 Experimental design
 
 ### 3.1 Recordings and reference
 
-Three real recordings, BY2, BY2H and BY2O, use the same robot installation. BY2 is the historical development and calibration sequence; parameters are transferred to the other two recordings. The windows last 274, 270 and 377 s, respectively. They include walking, turns and stationary behaviour, with differing antenna-state and motion conditions. The robot body IMU is the estimator’s inertial input. The commercial reference has its own internal inertial and visual fusion chain, but shares GNSS input lineage with the evaluated system.
-
